        "blockId": "syntax-concept",
        "dimensions": [
          "syntax",
          "concept"
        ],
        "text": "Could you help是礼貌请求；expedite的宾语是the review；without skipping any checks给加速方式设下边界。 加快可以来自减少等待、准备齐资料或协调人员。原句没有选定措施，也明确不能以省略检查换取速度。",
        "sourceRefs": [
          {
            "sourceId": "oewn-2025",
            "sourceVersion": "2025",
            "locator": "entries-e.json/expedite/v / expedite%2:41:00::",
            "supportedClaim": "speed up the progress of; facilitate",
            "url": "https://en-word.net/"
          }
        ],
        "title": "句子结构与当前所指"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "contrast",
        "dimensions": [
          "contrast"
        ],
        "text": "expedite是促进加速；skip是略过；rush可能暗示仓促。加快流程不必等于压缩证据要求。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "容易混淆的地方"
      },
      {
        "blockId": "game-neighbors",
        "dimensions": [
          "languageGame",
          "englishNeighbors"
        ],
        "text": "可找出等待或重复环节，说明能加快哪一步，并确认检查范围保持完整；让提速方案具体可评估。 expedite the review与remove waiting time相关；complete documentation可能减少往返；without skipping checks保留工作内容。",
        "sourceRefs": [],
        "title": "讨论通常怎样继续"
